#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133538 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b2c90d8-0f2e-5f84-bf67-7620d6f1d308" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Design Matrix When the Regression Curve Contains Zero Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "98ec57bb-04f5-559a-9057-854de19eda7f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5612" :question/problem "The vector of coefficients of the curve $y = \\beta_0 + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as\n\n| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $6$ | $3$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector. Find $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$ in this context." :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$\\color{blue}1$** | **$\\color{blue}2$** | **$\\color{blue}3$** | **$\\color{blue}4$** | **$\\color{blue}5$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $\\color{red}6$ | $\\color{red}3$ | $\\color{red}2$ | $\\color{red}4$ | $\\color{red}6$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve\n\n$$\ny = \\beta_0 + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution ${\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}}$ to the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1^{2} & 1^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2^{2} & 2^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3^{2} & 3^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4^{2} & 4^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5^{2} & 5^{3}\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(X)\\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(β) &= \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(y)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta$ is the parameter vector, and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133539 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d0f92926-0c15-554a-8fba-55b05d435980" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Expression for a Least-Squares Regression Curve"}] :question/id #uuid "f5354fe5-fa4b-5443-a097-40174b0b7b16" :question/math-academy-id "e-5613" :question/problem "Consider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression (in terms of $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$) for the vector of coefficients $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ of the curve $y=\\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3$ that best fits the data.\n\n| $x$ | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ | $2$ |\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0^{2} & 0^{3} \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1^{2} & 1^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2^{2} & 2^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3^{2} & 3^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4^{2} & 4^{3}\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the curve\n\n$$\ny=\\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution ${\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}}$ to the system\n\n$$\nX \\boldsymbol{\\beta} = \\mathbf{y}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ is the parameter vector, and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by $X^T$, we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\nX^T \\! X {\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}} = X^T \\mathbf{y}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X^T}X$ is invertible and\n\n$$\n{\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}} = (X^T \\! X)^{-1} X^T \\mathbf{y}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133558 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa5bf185-de29-5185-ba57-c64250332dfa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Polynomial Regression Model"}] :question/id #uuid "75c0086b-db74-5f01-8d66-f023dd7b575d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6094" :question/problem "The vector of coefficients of the curve $y = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as\n\n| $x$ | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** | **$6$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $40$ | $70$ | $120$ | $100$ | $80$ |\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{1} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector. Find $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$ in this context." :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$\\color{blue}2$** | **$\\color{blue}3$** | **$\\color{blue}4$** | **$\\color{blue}5$** | **$\\color{blue}6$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $\\color{red}40$ | $\\color{red}70$ | $\\color{red}120$ | $\\color{red}100$ | $\\color{red}80$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve\n\n$$\ny = \\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x + \\beta_2 x^2 + \\beta_3 x^3\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution ${\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}}$ to the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2^{2} & 2^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3^{2} & 3^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4^{2} & 4^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5 & 5^{2} & 5^{3} \\\\ 1 & 6 & 6^{2} & 6^{3}\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(X)\\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{1} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(β) &= \\begin{bmatrix}40 \\\\ 70 \\\\ 120 \\\\ 100 \\\\ 80\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(y)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta$ is the parameter vector, and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa5bf185-de29-5185-ba57-c64250332dfa" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Elements of a Polynomial Regression Model"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b48cc0c5-28f0-578c-b352-b186ebff8f42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132345} {:answer/id #uuid "bc2daba7-3a93-547d-bf04-a48a7bce73e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1^{2} & 1^{3} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2^{2} & 2^{3} \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3^{2} & 3^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4^{2} & 4^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5 & 5^{2} & 5^{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132346} {:answer/id #uuid "e7dfa58e-bb2b-5f4d-aa52-783cb8f4ef2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132347} {:answer/id #uuid "232fa400-ff29-55fd-a9e9-c9f3f2388208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132348} {:answer/id #uuid "755f0db9-f7f4-5793-9caf-f9f44a4d11ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "755f0db9-f7f4-5793-9caf-f9f44a4d11ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132349} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5055672-e9eb-5ff1-bfca-04e2ffeb7497" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132344}] :question/id #uuid "d9c9be89-da09-5bc3-a22f-a4017d770581" :question/math-academy-id "q-42412" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $-1$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y = β_{0} + β_{1}x + β_{2}x^{2} + β_{3}x^{3}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}β_{0} \\\\ β_{1} \\\\ β_{2} \\\\ β_{3}\\end{bmatrix} = (X^{T}X)^{-1}X^{T}y$,\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the observation vector $y$ in this context?"}]}
